# backup-alert.env.template — T05.4 EnvironmentFile TEMPLATE (deployment artifact)
#
# Copy this file to the production EnvironmentFile path referenced by
# infra/backup-alert.service:
#   /workspace/hpc-perf-platform/backend/scripts/backup_alert.env
#
# This template contains ONLY non-secret operational variables and placeholders.
# It carries NO credentials and NO real webhook URL. Do not commit a populated
# production env with secrets into version control.
#
# Owner / ApprovalTicket / Rollback are tracked in the .service file header and
# the change ticket — they are intentionally NOT filled here.
#
# Every variable has a built-in default inside backup_alert.sh, so you only need
# to set the values ops wants to override. Sensible production-typical defaults
# are shown below for review; adjust in the approved change window.

# Base directory for state/log/lock (default: /workspace/hpc-perf-platform).
BACKUP_ALERT_BASE=/workspace/hpc-perf-platform

# Where the daemon stores success/failure markers and sha256 state.
BACKUP_ALERT_STATE_DIR=/workspace/hpc-perf-platform/backup-alert.state

# Local alert log (used even when no webhook is configured).
BACKUP_ALERT_LOG=/workspace/hpc-perf-platform/backup-alert.log

# Single-instance lock file (requires `flock` on the target).
BACKUP_ALERT_LOCK=/workspace/hpc-perf-platform/backup-alert.lock

# RPO gate: a successful backup must be no older than this many seconds.
# T05.3 Round4 set the production RPO to 6 hours.
BACKUP_ALERT_MAX_AGE=21600

# Daemon check interval in seconds (how often `check` runs the freshness gate).
BACKUP_ALERT_INTERVAL=300

# Minimum seconds between two alerts of the same kind (avoids alert storms).
BACKUP_ALERT_COOLDOWN=3600

# Optional HTTPS webhook. LEAVE EMPTY to use the local alert log only.
# If external alerting is required, set the APPROVED endpoint in the change
# window — do NOT paste a real URL into this template/repo.
# BACKUP_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=<APPROVED_WEBHOOK_URL>
BACKUP_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional self-run backup command for `backup_alert.sh run`. Leave unset when
# an external scheduler (e.g. sync_prep_backup.sh) calls record-success /
# record-failure explicitly. The command sources the protected app env itself;
# do not embed credentials here.
# BACKUP_ALERT_COMMAND=/path/to/approved-production-backup-wrapper
